; coverage test for modal.kurt's dual form of "T" and its "box-def"/"diamond-def" axioms (see
; k-distribution.kurt's comment on the schema-variable bug these were part of) -- exercised here
; with a plain declared boolean `X`, not the file's own `p`/`A` example symbols.
; Given classical propositional logic and modal duality, `X implies ◇X` is equivalent to the
; standard T axiom `□X implies X`; it is not the seriality axiom D (`□X implies ◇X`).
load modal
bool X

use X
X ⇒ ◇X
◇X

use □X
□X ⇒ ¬◇¬X
¬◇¬X
